# Smart Traffic City Map Implementation Plan

Design and implement a multi-layered, zoom-based intelligent city map using `react-leaflet` to replace/enhance the current 2D grid simulation.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The current backend provides a 5x5 grid state without coordinates. I will map these 25 intersections to a real-world geographic area (e.g., downtown San Francisco) to provide the "Real-world city visualization" requested.
> [!NOTE]
> The "Detailed Intersection Simulation" (Zoom 18+) will be implemented using a Canvas overlay for high performance vehicle animations.

## Proposed Changes

### Dependencies
- Install `leaflet`, `react-leaflet`, and `@types/leaflet`.

---

### Components & State

#### [NEW] [CityMap.tsx](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/components/CityMap.tsx)
- Main map component using `MapContainer`.
- Implements dark-themed OpenStreetMap tiles.
- Handles zoom level detection via `map.getZoom()`.

#### [NEW] [IntersectionLayer.tsx](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/components/IntersectionLayer.tsx)
- Orchestrates the rendering of markers/overlays based on zoom level.
- **Zoom 12-14**: Heat circles (Green/Yellow/Red).
- **Zoom 15-17**: Glowing signal nodes.
- **Zoom 18+**: `SimulationOverlay`.

#### [NEW] [SimulationOverlay.tsx](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/components/SimulationOverlay.tsx)
- Custom Leaflet overlay using HTML5 Canvas or SVG.
- Renders 4 lanes, animated vehicles, and signal lights.
- Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth 60fps animations.

#### [MODIFY] [LiveMapView.tsx](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/components/LiveMapView.tsx)
- Integrate the new `CityMap` into the "Live Map" tab.
- Pass global traffic state (intersections, vehicles) to the map.

#### [MODIFY] [types.ts](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/types.ts)
- Update [IntersectionStatus](file:///c:/Users/H%20P/Desktop/uhackpro/signal-iq/types.ts#22-28) to include `lat`, `lng`, `density`, and `aiPrediction`.

---

### Features

#### Emergency Mode
- Draw a blue polyline route.
- Synchronize signal states along the route to "Green Corridor".

#### AI Optimization
- "Apply AI Optimization" button in the side panel.
- Visual feedback on the map (marker glow updates).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` to ensure TypeScript and Vite build pass.

### Manual Verification
1. Open the "Live Map" tab.
2. Verify zoom levels:
    - 12-14: Circle markers with density-based colors.
    - 15-17: Signal nodes with state indicators.
    - 18+: Detailed 2D lane-level simulation.
3. Click an intersection and verify the AI Optimization panel.
4. Toggle "Emergency Mode" and verify the blue route and green corridor.
5. Check performance during high vehicle density (zoom level 18+).
